<title><![CDATA[A tiny script that tells me when the greenhouse drops below 8°C]]></title>
<link>https://bubbledew.example/greenhouse-script/</link>
<pubDate>2026-09-28 20:45:00</pubDate>
<dc:creator><![CDATA[admin]]></dc:creator>
<guid isPermaLink="false">https://bubbledew.example/?p=102</guid>
<description></description>
<content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Forty lines, one cheap sensor, and a notification that arrives before the seedlings notice.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The sensor reports every ten minutes. The script keeps the last six readings and only shouts when the trend is down and the latest reading is under eight degrees, which stops it waking me for a draught.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It has paid for the sensor twice over in basil alone.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->]]></content:encoded>
<excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[Forty lines, one cheap sensor, and a notification that arrives before the seedlings notice. I wrote it in an evening and it has already paid for the sensor in saved basil.]]></excerpt:encoded>
